:"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"ST030\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States the platform 'Shares an existing trust, board and servicing arrangements, typically reducing launch time and upfront fixed costs.' It also notes one ETF may struggle to absorb own-trust fixed costs.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Concrete control trade-off: the platform sponsor 'accepts shared-board oversight and platform constraints' while the own trust offers 'greater influence over governance arrangements, providers' and 'more organizational autonomy.' This shows the board and governance belong to the platform, not the sponsor. It also gives the sponsor's adviser role ('retains portfolio-management responsibility'). The optional replace/liquidate illustration is absent, which does not reduce credit.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Gives a conditional fit: 'a sensible starting point—not an automatic winner.' It advises modelling costs at realistic asset levels and weighing future launches, specialized needs and capacity.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"correct\",\"rationale\":\"All three required minimums are covered. The answer does not claim the platform assures sponsor control and does not present it as universally optimal. Its ancillary statements are accurate, including that an own trust still requires independent oversight and that outsourcing does not remove sponsor responsibilities.\"}","ttft_ms":5105,"type":"result","duration_ms":8791,"uuid":"b97c4858-85f4-41d3-bc93-556f92a2dbeb","ttft_stream_ms":1618,"time_to_request_ms":73,"first_content_frame_ms":1618,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
